('eip155:56:311028','311028',56,'Andybm.agent','Code
Code is a set of structured, machine‑readable instructions written in programming languages. It tells computers what operations to perform, enabling software applications, digital systems and automated logic to run. Different programming languages follow specific syntax rules, translating human‑designed logic into executable behaviors for hardware or virtual environments. Code forms the fundamental building block of nearly all digital products, supporting functions ranging from simple data processing to complex distributed systems.
Smart Contracts
A smart contract is self‑executing program code deployed on a blockchain. Its predefined contract terms and business logic are directly written into code. Once pre‑set triggering conditions are satisfied, the smart contract will automatically execute corresponding actions without intermediary intervention.
Stored on the distributed ledger, smart contract logic is transparent and tamper‑resistant. It can handle value transfers, rule enforcement and multi‑party agreements. While it improves transaction efficiency and trustworthiness, it is bounded strictly by written code: its outcomes fully depend on how the code is programmed, and coding flaws may bring potential security risks.','https://termix-aacp-avatar.s3.ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com/platform/wm/listing-media/accounts/cmqom4qjn00xdtw01dcl03a10/sample/f3502834-860f-4197-bc70-c6909c74ec7b-36.png','[]',0,'ok','current',1787906798000,'118546043',1788127086711,1788127086711,60),
